AirWing was relicensed from MIT to GPL-3.0 to incorporate an AirPlay
screen-mirroring implementation, including the FairPlay SAP authentication
handshake required by Apple TV. That component is a clean-room TypeScript
reimplementation whose FairPlay white-box constants and algorithm are derived
from prior reverse-engineering published under the GPL:

  - doubletake (https://github.com/omarroth/doubletake), GPL-3.0, an AirPlay
    mirroring sender for Linux.
  - UxPlay (https://github.com/FDH2/UxPlay), GPL-3.0, and the playfair lineage
    (RPiPlay, shairport) it builds on.

FairPlay is a trademark of Apple Inc. AirWing is not affiliated with, authorized
or endorsed by Apple. The FairPlay SAP handshake is reproduced solely to allow a
user to mirror their own screen to hardware they own (interoperability).
